// The Dogger Bank, 24 January 1915 at 07:50 GMT: Hipper's raid toward the Dogger Bank has run into the Harwich Force at
// dawn and, seeing Beatty's smoke, he has turned for home, south-east at the speed of his slowest, Blücher. Beatty's
// five battlecruisers chase fourteen miles astern, the faster ones slowly overhauling; Goodenough's light cruisers on
// his bow, Tyrwhitt's destroyers astern of the Germans, the German light cruisers and torpedo boats about Hipper.
// A stern chase, then the battle. History's forces, the destroyers thinned; the classes are stand-ins (lion for Lion
// and Princess Royal, tiger_1914, indefatigable for New Zealand, invincible for Indomitable; the towns, arethusa,
// l_laforey and m_class; seydlitz, moltke, derfflinger, armoured_cruiser for Blücher, graudenz and stettin, v1 and v25):
//   Britain, the hunters: five battlecruisers, the faster three overhauling, 13.5 in guns; thin armour, and the
//   signals that went wrong in history are the player's to get right.
//   Germany, the quarry: three battlecruisers and the old Blücher holding them back, armour that takes punishment,
//   torpedo boats to throw at the chase; and home a long way off.
// The weather of the day: clear, a light north-easterly, a calm sea.
